---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Sources & Methodology — ExpertNetworks.net">
  <section class="pt-32 pb-24 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-accent text-sm font-medium no-underline mb-8 hover:underline">
        &larr; Home
      </a>

      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-primary mb-8">Sources & Methodology</h1>

      <div class="prose prose-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed space-y-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary">How We Gather Data</h2>
        <p>Network profiles are compiled from publicly available information including company websites, press releases, industry reports, regulatory filings, and third-party news coverage. We do not use proprietary or confidential data.</p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary">Data Points We Track</h2>
        <p>Each network profile includes the following where available:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>Company name, headquarters, and founding year</li>
          <li>Approximate expert count and employee count</li>
          <li>Core services and AI capabilities</li>
          <li>Industries served and geographic focus</li>
          <li>Pricing model</li>
          <li>Key differentiators</li>
          <li>Compliance approach (MNPI policies, vetting procedures)</li>
          <li>Best-fit buyer persona (PE, consulting, hedge fund, corporate)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary">Expert Counts & Employee Numbers</h2>
        <p>These figures are approximate and typically sourced from company websites, LinkedIn, press releases, and industry reports. Expert counts in particular are self-reported by networks and vary in definition — some count registered experts, others count active or vetted experts. We report the most commonly cited figure and note the source date.</p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary">News Curation</h2>
        <p>Industry news is curated from third-party journalism, industry reports, and analyst coverage. We label the source of each article. Where a news item originates from a press release wire service (e.g., Business Wire, PR Newswire), we label it as such — these are company-originated announcements distributed via paid channels, not independent reporting.</p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary">What We Exclude</h2>
        <p>We aim to exclude self-promotional content disguised as news. However, we may include company announcements when they contain material facts (funding rounds, acquisitions, product launches) and we label them honestly as company-sourced.</p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary">Corrections & Updates</h2>
        <p>If you identify inaccurate information on this site, please reach out. We review corrections promptly and update profiles with a new "last updated" timestamp. Each profile shows when it was last reviewed.</p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary">Inclusion Criteria</h2>
        <p>To be listed on ExpertNetworks.net, a company must:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>Operate primarily as an expert network (connecting clients with subject-matter experts)</li>
          <li>Have a public-facing website with verifiable information</li>
          <li>Be actively operating (not defunct or acquired without a successor product)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not charge for inclusion and do not accept payment for favorable profiles.</p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-primary">Limitations</h2>
        <p>This site does not yet cover the full landscape of 100+ active expert networks globally. We are expanding coverage and prioritize accuracy over quantity. Our current directory is a growing subset, not an exhaustive list.</p>

        <p class="text-xs text-tertiary mt-8">Last updated: March 2026</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
